PROTOCOL 6354922fcc49e9033c76212021af914c52a9321a7af8b256ed88f1029415b279 MANIFEST 4bfe7451a41b853042f181cbcd7c326649b4222279bc35dd9787afa38c8d4033 221 files; newly cited manifest files: ['framelease_v4/analysis/tests/test_verify_table1_extra.py', 'framelease_v4/analysis/verify_table1_extra.py']
**Amendment A11, 2026-11-15 07:51 (Beijing time): registration of the independent recomputation of the Table I columns
GPU usage, DMR, action age, fallback ratio, EIR and P_both and of the closed-loop R_cond (Secs. 7.2, 9.12, 9.13; no
effect on any run, job file, selection or criterion).**
* Cause. Sec. 7.2 lists GPU usage, DMR, action age p50 and p95, fallback ratio, EIR and P_both as columns of Table I and
  puts the closed-loop R_cond in the table notes or the text; Sec. 9.13 puts every registered result in the paper or its
  supplement; Sec. 9.12 requires an independent recomputation of the Table I columns from the raw run directories before
  any number enters the paper. Amendment A10 registers `verify_independent.py`, which recomputes DS, SR, RC,
  collisions/km and infractions/km, and leaves the other columns to a second independent script registered by its own
  amendment before the analysis freeze (Amendment A10, deviation 9). This entry registers that script and its tests.
  Item R7B built it from the PROTOCOL text and the data formats, independently of the aggregator, the analysis and the
  implementation of these metrics (Sec. 9.12; `outputs/framelease_v4/build/R7B/`). The review returned GO_WITH_FIXES;
  must-fix M1-M5 and should-fix S1-S5 are applied, and the review of the fixes returned GO. From this entry on, a change
  of either file is an amendment.
* Change: the files, their roles and the PROTOCOL sections they implement.

  | file | role | PROTOCOL | review |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `framelease_v4/analysis/verify_table1_extra.py` | the recomputation, per run from the raw logs, of GPU usage (and CUDA-seconds per second), DMR (from the first commit on; the all-ticks and expired-only variants), action age p50 and p95, the fallback ratio and episodes, P_both, EIR and the closed-loop R_cond (also without the V = 0 plans), and its comparison with the aggregator's `runs.csv` and `arm_summary.csv`, the runtime's `summary.json`, the runner's END-line results and the analysis outputs; the Sec. 9.11 guard | 5.1, 5.8, 6.2-6.4, 7.2, 9.11-9.13 | `build/R7B/review/REVIEW.md`: GO_WITH_FIXES, must-fix M1-M5 and should-fix S1-S5 applied; `build/R7B/rereview/REVIEW.md`: GO |
  | `framelease_v4/analysis/tests/test_verify_table1_extra.py` | known answers on synthetic run directories, the run-level and analysis-level comparisons, the Sec. 6.3 definitions, the actor-log decoder, the guard, the imports, and the P1-0 smoke runs against their `summary.json` | as above | as above |

* What it computes (its docstring fixes every definition; the route is the unit, arm-level values are means over
  routes).
  * Inputs: the runner's `status.jsonl` (the last final 'end' record of a job names its run directory) and, in each run
    directory, `config.json`, `raw/agent/framelease/{ticks,jobs,events,decisions}.jsonl`, `summary.json` where present,
    the actor-box log `raw/agent/framelease/actors.jsonl.gz` and the lease parameter file that the config names.
  * GPU usage: the union of the cost-model intervals of prefixes and flow steps (`jobs.jsonl`; for a job still running
    at the end, its `job_start` event and the step quanta in the ticks) over the span of the ticks.
  * DMR: the ticks from the first commit on whose committed action, rebuilt from the accepted commit events, is not
    valid by the arm's rule (before the deadline for the lease arms; below the age cap for Fixed Deep, Fast Only and
    Event-Triggered), over those ticks. Fallback ratio: the ticks in mode 'fallback' over all ticks. Action age: the
    tick time minus the capture time of the committed action over the tracked ticks, p50 and p95 by linear
    interpolation. P_both: the decision rows at depth >= 1 with the shield evaluated and two feasible actions, over
    those rows.
  * EIR and the closed-loop R_cond (Sec. 6.3, standard validity): every accepted commit is a committed plan, placed
    with the true capture pose of the actor-box log; the ego footprint is the lease footprint of Eqs. 1-3 (headings by
    central differences, the ego box of the lease parameter file); the actor boxes are those of the log at t_k + tau.
    V is the first time at which the footprint comes within d_safe = 0.5 m of an actor box (the first conflicting
    sample of the 0.05 s grid brackets it; bisection refines it to 1e-4 s) and V_suf = clip(V - T_c, 0, H_bar). A
    conflict plan is a miss when H > V_suf; EIR counts the tracked ticks whose committed plan is a conflict plan at an
    age of at least V_suf. Plans that cannot be evaluated and the time resolution of V give bounds.
  * Not recomputed: the CIs and p-values of the contrasts of these metrics (the S-dmr family and the secondary rows;
    their per-route values and means are compared), the ability membership of the per-ability rows, and the
    closed-loop lease utilization and premature expiry (Sec. 6.3; not columns of Table I).
* Independence. Standard library, `zlib` and numpy only. It imports nothing of `framelease_v4/analysis`,
  `framelease_v4/arms/metrics_v4.py`, `realized.py`, `actor_log.py` or `framelease_v2` and uses no code of them: the
  definitions follow the PROTOCOL text and the documented conventions of the lease footprint, its own RFC 1952 decoder
  reads the gzip members of the actor-box log, and only data formats are taken from elsewhere. The block comparison of
  the review (`build/R7B/review/scripts/blocks.py`) finds no shared block of four or more lines with these files other
  than import lists; must-fix M3 removed the one copied block.
* Tolerances (in the docstring: stated before the first comparison of each part; the time resolution of V with must-fix
  M1). Counts are compared exactly; fractions, ratios and times at 1e-6 absolute (the mean episode count at 1e-9). A
  value with bounds (the in-flight step quanta of a job still running at the end; Sec. 6.3: the unevaluable plans and
  the plans with |H - V_suf| < 1e-3 s) agrees when the other side lies within the bounds widened by the tolerance;
  these agreements are counted by kind. A difference below the registered grid (1e-4 for fractions, 1 ms for ages) is
  flagged 'below_grid' and remains a difference. An expected column, field or file that is absent is a difference.
  Every comparison has a scope: 'analysis' for a value the analysis reads for a column of Table I, 'record' for every
  other value; the verdict counts every difference.
* Interim looks (Sec. 9.11). Before any log is read, every input that names a route is classified with the registered
  route split (runner records, `runs.csv` rows, run directories, the jobs of `cells.csv` and every route list of the
  analysis outputs); an input whose route is unknown counts as a registered test route. A test route is released only
  by a valid analysis-freeze record that covers the input (its sha256 cited in Sec. 13, PROTOCOL.md equal to its seal,
  the recorded route split and analysis code on disk); otherwise the run is refused (exit 4) and only
  `guard_log.jsonl` is written. Under the registered record (status 'final') every run directory is recomputed: the
  development option `--runs-csv-values` is refused there. The test options `--route-split`, `--protocol` and `--seal`
  apply to synthetic test routes only.
* Development data (Secs. 9.11, 9.12; `build/` stands for `outputs/framelease_v4/build/`). No test-route run existed or
  was read; the values were used to check the code, never to choose a definition, a tolerance or a rule. Synthetic run
  directories with known answers (the tests); with `--runs-csv-values`, the synthetic analysis outputs
  `build/R7/dev/syn_r4/`, `build/R7/dev/syn_varied/` and `build/R6/dev_inputs/`; the 14 P1-0 smoke run directories of
  training route 18305 (the tests); and the P1 training-route run directories named by two copies of the `queue_p1`
  runner records (`build/R7/dev/p1_snapshot/`, made on 2026-11-14 at 11:46; `build/R7B/dev/p1_snap_2203/`, made on
  2026-11-14 at 22:03), compared with the development aggregations `build/R7/dev/agg_p1/`, `build/R7B/dev/agg_now/`
  and `build/R7B/dev/agg_snap_2203/` (Amendment A10, deviation 1), from 2026-11-14 14:39 to 2026-11-15 01:13, into
  `build/R7B/dev/verify_p1*/` and scratch directories under /tmp (`build/R7B/PROGRESS.md`). The definitions and
  tolerances were fixed in the docstring before the first comparison; the corrections of must-fix M1 and M2 (the
  continuous V, the lease footprint) follow the text of Sec. 6.3.
* Development comparison of the registered version (2026-11-15 01:13, `build/R7B/dev/verify_p1_snap_2203_c/`). On the
  P1 runs of `build/R7B/dev/p1_snap_2203/` against `build/R7B/dev/agg_snap_2203/` (the aggregator of Amendment A3):
  180 run directories recomputed, 179 `runs.csv` rows with analysis_use, 12,259 comparisons, 136 differences, 1 of them
  in a value the analysis reads. Every difference has a recorded cause (`build/R7B/PROGRESS.md`;
  `build/R7B/dev/reconcile_p1_c.json` for Sec. 6.3): the cross-check columns `gpu_usage_recomputed` and
  `gpu_busy_recomputed_s` and the commit count of `runs.csv` omit the work of a job still running at the end of a run
  (the `gpu_usage` that the analysis reads agrees within the in-flight bounds); the timed-out run of job
  `v4p1_fl_heuristic_B0_d10_k1.0_s11_r23659` (not used; no `summary.json`) has empty cells there; the Sec. 6.3 counts
  of 19 runs differ by finding F1, which also gives the one difference the analysis reads (`fast_only`, route 1792:
  EIR 94/412 = 0.2282 recomputed, 85/412 = 0.2063 in `runs.csv`); 2 runs agree only within the Sec. 6.3 bounds
  (finding F2; one miss within the time resolution of V). `summary.json`: 3,759 comparisons, 0 differences. On the
  synthetic analysis outputs (`--runs-csv-values`; `build/R7B/dev/syn_r4_c/`, `r6_dev_inputs_c/`, `syn_varied_c/`):
  AGREE with 25,746, 25,746 and 20,242 comparisons.
* Findings about registered files (Sec. 6.3), carried to the analysis freeze; this entry changes neither file.
  * F1. `framelease_v4/arms/actor_log.py` places a row of the actor-box log at its frame time, and `realized.py` treats
    a time above the last row by more than 1e-9 s as outside the log, while the plan sample times `capture_s + tau`
    carry the runtime's offset of 3e-7 to 1.1e-6 s: a sample that lands on the last row has no actors, and a plan whose
    horizon ends at that row counts as log-censored. On the P1 runs above this changes the Sec. 6.3 counts of 19 runs
    (38 plans log-censored there and clear here; 2 conflict plans missed there) and one EIR value the analysis reads.
  * F2. `realized.py` places a plan only through the actor-log row of its capture step: a plan without that row (a
    decimated log) and the commits of a job still running at the end leave the counts and, with their tracked ticks,
    the EIR denominator, which Sec. 6.3 forms from all tracked ticks. No P1 log was decimated; the recomputation
    reports such values within its bounds.
  The recomputation reports every value that F1 changes as a difference; its cause is entered with the result (use
  rule 2).
* Use of the registered files (fixed by this entry).
  1. After the analysis freeze is entered and `analyze_v4.py` has written `final_<stamp>/analysis/` (Amendment A10, use
     rule 1), an independent session (Sec. 9.12) runs `verify_table1_extra.py` next to `verify_independent.py`
     (Amendment A10, use rule 4): with `--analysis-freeze` (the record, or the `final_<stamp>/` directory that holds
     it), one `--queue` for every queue whose job lines the aggregation covers, `--agg final_<stamp>/`,
     `--analysis final_<stamp>/analysis/` and `--out` a new directory such as
     `outputs/framelease_v4/verification/final_<stamp>_table1_extra/`; never with `--runs-csv-values` or a test option.
     Only a result with status 'final' in `table1_extra.json` counts.
  2. AGREE releases the Table I columns GPU usage, DMR, action age p50 and p95, fallback ratio, EIR and P_both and the
     closed-loop R_cond (table notes or text). On DIFFER every difference is resolved and its cause entered in Sec. 13
     before any of these numbers enters the paper.
  3. The sha256 of `table1_extra.json` and of the `SHA256SUMS` of that directory are entered in their own dated Sec. 13
     entry before the paper is written.
* In-place text. Sec. 9.12, "**Verification.**" (as Amendment A10 leaves it): "a second script, registered by its own
  amendment before the analysis freeze, recomputes the other Table I columns," becomes "Amendment A11:
  `framelease_v4/analysis/verify_table1_extra.py` recomputes GPU usage, DMR, action age p50 and p95, fallback ratio,
  EIR, P_both and the closed-loop R_cond,".
* Scope. No run, job file, pin, stage selection, freeze or criterion changes. No job line pins these files, no agent
  process imports them, and neither the aggregator nor the analysis imports them; the analysis-freeze record does not
  list them. This entry precedes the analysis freeze; the phase driver's gate G8 waits for Amendment A10 only.
